{
  "id": 474367659,
  "iid": 24394,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTPS: Fix DATA_FRAG reassembly when submessage has multiple fragments",
  "description": "fragment_add_check was always reading fragment data from offset (the\nstart of the first fragment in the submessage) instead of\noffset + (frag_index_in_submessage * frag_size). The second and\nsubsequent fragments were getting the first fragment's bytes, corrupting\nthe reassembled tail.\n\nAlso reset param_length_length to 2 at the top of each parameter\niteration. PID_EXTENDED sets it to 4 and that value must not persist\ninto the next parameter, which caused PID_SENTINEL to go unrecognized\nafter large parameters like PID_TYPE_OBJECT_LB.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (Copilot)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-15T20:23:46.526Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-16T05:11:42.124Z",
